# Module 2.1 – Security Assessments

## Overview
Basic cybersecurity tools and concepts used to assess system security.

## Vulnerability Scanners
Identify weaknesses in systems:
- Weak passwords
- Missing patches
- Open ports
- Misconfigurations

Examples: Nessus, Nmap

## Types of Scans
- Network scans → devices and ports
- Application scans → app security
- Web scans → website issues

Credentialed = deeper scan  
Non-credentialed = external view

## Command Line Tools
- ping → test connection
- ipconfig → network info
- tracert → route tracking
- nslookup → DNS lookup
- netstat → open connections
- nmap → network scanning

## SIEM vs SOAR
SIEM → detects and monitors threats  
SOAR → automates response and handling

## Key Takeaways
- Scanners find system risks early
- Tools help troubleshoot networks
- SIEM = detection
- SOAR = response
